  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-31 by an independent auditor who authored none of faf7c5c380. RFC 2545 Section 3: \"The value of the Length of Next Hop Network Address field on a MP_REACH_NLRI attribute shall be set to 16, when only a global address is present, or 32 if a link-local address is also included in the Next Hop field.\" faf7c5c380 (filter chain model moved into internal/component/policy) changed one line in the tagged unit internal/component/bgp/reactor/rfc2545_forward_subnet_test.go::TestRFC2545EffectivePairPolicyAndMixedSibling: mustPolicy(t, []filterapi.FilterRef{{Name: \"ipv6:raw-next-hop\"}}, filterapi.FinalAccept) became mustPolicy(t, []routepolicy.Ref{{Name: \"ipv6:raw-next-hop\"}}, routepolicy.FinalAccept). mustPolicy still calls filterapi.NewPolicy with the same single unbound ref and the explicit accept final (NewPolicy now wraps policy.NewChain; an unbound ref stays external as the zero inProcess field did), so the policy the fixture installs, every input and every assertion are unchanged. No other commit touched the file since the verdict was stamped. The unit still inspects the complete emitted native next-hop field per case, so a wrong length still fails it. Every other tagged carrier is byte-identical and its judgement stands. Verdict unchanged: enforced. Ran: go test -tags ze_bgp -run over the six faf7c5c380-changed reactor units, PASS on 2026-10-31. Earlier judgements are in this file's git history.",
